@dkayiwa The `modifyColumn` change was dropped from Liquibase (actually in 2.0) and moved into a standard extension for backwards compatibility with 1.x. The Liquibase team thought it was better replaced by using the `modifyDataType` change (and other changes like `addNotNull` as necessary). In the 3.x series, the standard extension was completely dropped. I'm kind of surprised you don't get some sort of error, though.

OpenMRS had previously forked with extension with some small changes (one of the Liquibase extensions we had), but even that is obsolete and needs to be rewritten for 3.x. I made an attempt to do so a while ago, which I shared [here](https://github.com/ibacher/openmrs-core/commit/9c186a978d7e45053adabbe9b6f6876427cd5409).

This shouldn't be necessary for core to work (I think we only made use of this extension in 2.0), but it will be necessary for most modules to work, since it's used very extensively there (yay! technical debt!). The alternative that I thought of was simply to replace every use of `modifyColumn` with the corresponding other commands, but that's a pretty tall order as it's very widely used and it definitely affect the checksum.

