This isn't primarily about readability.

```java
log.debug("looking for un-run change sets in snapshot version '{}'", version);
```

Is essentially the equivalent of:

```java
if (log.isDebugEnabled()) {
    log.debug(String.format("looking for un-run change sets in snapshot version '%s'", version)); 
}
```

The advantage is that if `debug` level logging is not enabled for the logger, Hotspot will convert this to a NO-OP. Not a big deal for a few lines, but across a large-scale project in can add up. [Hence our coding convention](https://wiki.openmrs.org/display/docs/Java+Conventions#JavaConventions-loggingLogging).

This might be clearer using the streams API:

```java
// note the change from isVintageChangeSet -> isNotVintageChangeSet, but see below
return changeSets.stream().filter(this::isNotVintageChangeSet).collect(Collectors.toList());
```
